{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/107830-the-usage-of-high-rank-angels","id":107830,"title":"The Usage of High Rank Angels","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-07T18:27:49-07:00","id":107830,"title":"The Usage of High Rank Angels","content":"Hi all,<br /> <br /> So recently I read the final PDF version of Demon (my previous read through had been the preview text on the Kickstarter page) and got a POD version of the God Machine Chronicles book with my Kickstarter backer discount. <br /> <br /> I noticed a lot of sample angels in both books are between rank 1-3. There are examples of Rank 4+ Angels obviously, but they are kinda rare. I can list three off the top of my head:<br /> <br /> Y2K from Demon's core (Rank 4) <br /> Black Nathaniel from the GMC book (Rank 5)<br /> Triage from GMC book (Rank 6) <br /> <br /> Now, I know the issue of the implementation of Angels in a Demon game is a complex issue anyway.<br /> <br /> Namely that each ST has to decide where on the <i><b>&quot;There are always more Angels&quot;</b></i> vs <i><b>&quot;Its a big deal for the God Machine to make/summon and Angel&quot;</b></i> scale they rest. As both of these are themes within the game. <br /> <br /> Likewise, I know there is some issue with the fact that Demons are actually far more versatile then Angels as written mainly due to Angels being modeled using the PFR system for Spirits. Some people I have seen argue that a Demon with a good junk of XP is more then able to handle any angel below Rank 4. I'm not so sure about that myself, as while Angles might lack the power spread of Demons (at least for now, I imagine every splat book for Demon will include more Angelic Numina) the raw dice pools that a Rank 4 or 5 Demon can be rolling can just overpower most things (30+ dice will do that).<br /> <br /> Also added into this that if the Demon gains the right condition the its up the ST what servant of the God-Machine shows up to hunt them. One of the options is of course a single Rank 4 or 5 Angel.<br /> <br /> So I was kinda wondering if people have brought out Rank 4 or 5 Angels a lot in their Demon games? As I have yet to run or play in a game I have no practical experience with this aspect, but I find it interesting to see how often other ST's might bring out a serious opponent as the result of Cover issues. <br /> <br /> Also I am curious and interested to hear about what new Rank 4 and 5 Angels people have come up with for their games. Since these are the Angels most likely to have more fleshed out characters it seem, or at least thats implied by some of the fluff in the Demon book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T18:36:02-07:00","id":107834,"title":"","content":"I have yet to dream up a scenario that would warrant a rank 5 angel. Those things are on par with most True Fae Actors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T22:40:49-07:00","id":107989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/107830-the-usage-of-high-rank-angels#post107830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi all,<br /> <br /> <br /> Likewise, I know there is some issue with the fact that Demons are actually far more versatile then Angels as written mainly due to Angels being modeled using the PFR system for Spirits. Some people I have seen argue that a Demon with a good junk of XP is more then able to handle any angel below Rank 4. I'm not so sure about that myself, as while Angles might lack the power spread of Demons (at least for now, I imagine every splat book for Demon will include more Angelic Numina) the raw dice pools that a Rank 4 or 5 Demon can be rolling can just overpower most things (30+ dice will do that).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's a point to be made about how every single Embed can be a Numina. Though some of them Angels don't need. They're explicitly powers that the splat shares with Angels, and there's even examples of Angels with Embeds. So that's something!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/107830-the-usage-of-high-rank-angels#post107830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also added into this that if the Demon gains the right condition the its up the ST what servant of the God-Machine shows up to hunt them. One of the options is of course a single Rank 4 or 5 Angel.<br /> <br /> So I was kinda wondering if people have brought out Rank 4 or 5 Angels a lot in their Demon games? As I have yet to run or play in a game I have no practical experience with this aspect, but I find it interesting to see how often other ST's might bring out a serious opponent as the result of Cover issues.<br /> <br /> Also I am curious and interested to hear about what new Rank 4 and 5 Angels people have come up with for their games. Since these are the Angels most likely to have more fleshed out characters it seem, or at least thats implied by some of the fluff in the Demon book.</div> </div> </div> </div>My girlfriend and I have had one Angel in a story so far, and he was Rank 3. I'd be interested to hear more about these sorts of Angels too. I want to run Demon sometime in the future, but I also want to use the included adventure to teach my players and myself how to play Demon. I'm thinking that I'll need to pull one of these babies out eventually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T05:00:08-07:00","id":108104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Likewise, I know there is some issue with the fact that Demons are actually far more versatile then Angels as written mainly due to Angels being modeled using the PFR system for Spirits. Some people I have seen argue that a Demon with a good junk of XP is more then able to handle any angel below Rank 4. I'm not so sure about that myself, as while Angles might lack the power spread of Demons (at least for now, I imagine every splat book for Demon will include more Angelic Numina) the raw dice pools that a Rank 4 or 5 Demon can be rolling can just overpower most things (30+ dice will do that). </div> </div> </div> Umm..... I don't know where these people are getting their ideas from, but... a Rank 5 angel is generally scary. It has enough stats to absorb the damage from an attack that deals 10 damage in a single turn. And the essence to not only heal it all, but respond with an attack that could kill a demon without defenses in a single attack as well. Remember, Rank 5 angels have an average of 12~15 in each stat. That means that they can have up to 25 health at the high end, before any powers that boost health.<br /> <br /> <br /> And remember that they can get the same Embeds and Exploits as Numina that a Demon can. Its quite common in any game - ghosts can get Manifestation powers as numina, astrals/supernals getting mage rotes, spirits getting werewolf gifts. So, you pump out your Demon with 30+ dice to attack an angel (assuming its manifested in some meaningful way the demon can actually hurt the thing!) and it uses Just Bruised. 1 damage. How about take that huge amount of damage, then touch a demon with Shift Consequences. All that damage, gone, and into the demon's body? Ouch.<br /> <br /> And, like I said, that's assuming that the Demon can strike the angel in question. Angels aren't dumb - they're not going to materialize in a way the demon can easily &quot;kill them.&quot; Note that ephemerals are a lot harder to permanently kill, as they need to be robbed of essence as well to kill. Angels, also tend to want to hunt the demons, and shred their Covers. Or, heaven forbid, an ambush. Any scenario where a rank 5 being is &quot;easily killed&quot; is one where people are setting up white room, D&amp;D esk encounters and expecting the &quot;monsters&quot; to be idiots and just stand there, or use dumb tactics, before their power builds.<br /> <br /> The simple truth is that whomever told you that angels can't match up to a demon is simply full of hot air. Angels can do everything a demon can, plus access to more Numina and Influences that a Demon cannot. They have better stats, they have bodies that regenerate upon destruction. They've access to the backup systems of the God Machine, who can simply download new powers, information, aid, you name it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also I am curious and interested to hear about what new Rank 4 and 5 Angels people have come up with for their games. Since these are the Angels most likely to have more fleshed out characters it seem, or at least that's implied by some of the fluff in the Demon book. </div> </div> </div> I've got a rank 5 angel that's watching over a major city that's a giant Infrastructure being built towards a huge occult matrix. It's got a lot of underlings too.<br /> <br /> The idea here is that, since the God-Machine itself is basically a supernatural internet, built upon thousands and thousands of servers and nodes and connections, it can never really have a face. So, Mr Rank 5 Angel is actually a stand in for the leader of the angel army of the local city instead of the big GM. He's the face, the director, of all this. Also, the Linchpin.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T08:48:46-07:00","id":108228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/107830-the-usage-of-high-rank-angels?p=108104#post108104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've got a rank 5 angel that's watching over a major city that's a giant Infrastructure being built towards a huge occult matrix. It's got a lot of underlings too.<br /> <br /> The idea here is that, since the God-Machine itself is basically a supernatural internet, built upon thousands and thousands of servers and nodes and connections, it can never really have a face. So, Mr Rank 5 Angel is actually a stand in for the leader of the angel army of the local city instead of the big GM. He's the face, the director, of all this. Also, the Linchpin.</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes sense - but keep in mind that doing this changes the setting and theme of your setting. In this scenario, the god machine becomes an understandable entity rather than a malevolent, alien force. Part of the fun of making an adventure against the god machine is plotting random events that don't really make sense and never being able to get the big picture, but this changes it so that yes, one entity can and does understand what's going on.<br /> <br /> An idea I had for a setting is to take a city (Toronto) and throw in several high ranking angels with competing agendas - all trying to compete for resources on a large scale for different projects. These angels have only a vague idea that they're actually fighting each other in a weird, city wide A-B test from hell. There would of course be other entities in the city (Vampires, maybe some Geists) but the adventure will ultimately revolve around the demons figuring out that even if they bring down one infrastructure, two other projects greedily gobble up the resources and become more powerful. Ultimately, they can't face off against the big bads head on (they're too powerful) but they could find ways to play the angels against each other and use the GM against itself. The GM itself would still play a part, enacting smaller operations in the midst of this huge, long term infrastructure that is the city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T09:18:37-07:00","id":108248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/107830-the-usage-of-high-rank-angels?p=108104#post108104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Umm..... I don't know where these people are getting their ideas from, but... a Rank 5 angel is generally scary. It has enough stats to absorb the damage from an attack that deals 10 damage in a single turn. And the essence to not only heal it all, but respond with an attack that could kill a demon without defenses in a single attack as well. Remember, Rank 5 angels have an average of 12~15 in each stat. That means that they can have up to 25 health at the high end, before any powers that boost health.<br /> <br /> And remember that they can get the same Embeds and Exploits as Numina that a Demon can. Its quite common in any game - ghosts can get Manifestation powers as numina, astrals/supernals getting mage rotes, spirits getting werewolf gifts. So, you pump out your Demon with 30+ dice to attack an angel (assuming its manifested in some meaningful way the demon can actually hurt the thing!) and it uses Just Bruised. 1 damage. How about take that huge amount of damage, then touch a demon with Shift Consequences. All that damage, gone, and into the demon's body? Ouch.<br /> <br /> And, like I said, that's assuming that the Demon can strike the angel in question. Angels aren't dumb - they're not going to materialize in a way the demon can easily &quot;kill them.&quot; Note that ephemerals are a lot harder to permanently kill, as they need to be robbed of essence as well to kill. Angels, also tend to want to hunt the demons, and shred their Covers. Or, heaven forbid, an ambush. Any scenario where a rank 5 being is &quot;easily killed&quot; is one where people are setting up white room, D&amp;D esk encounters and expecting the &quot;monsters&quot; to be idiots and just stand there, or use dumb tactics, before their power builds.<br /> <br /> The simple truth is that whomever told you that angels can't match up to a demon is simply full of hot air. Angels can do everything a demon can, plus access to more Numina and Influences that a Demon cannot. They have better stats, they have bodies that regenerate upon destruction. They've access to the backup systems of the God Machine, who can simply download new powers, information, aid, you name it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I may not have been clear enough in my post. The reference to 30+ dice was in regard to a Rank 4 or 5 Angel, as they usually have 10-15 in a stat. My argument was that while Angels might be less versatile then Demons (and I'll get onto that in a second) they pack more of raw punch at the high end of things. <br /> <br /> Yes the fact that they are ephemeral is very , very good. Please correct me if I am wrong but I do believe that even when manifested ephemeral creatures like Angels only take bashing damage from everything that is not a bane, ban or supernatural attack? Also that to properly kill one you need to drain all its essence and then fill all its corpus with agg damage. Otherwise it just reforms at the Infrastructure that spawned it (in the case of Angels). <br /> <br /> I believe I have that correct right? <br /> <br /> I was under the impression that Exploits were explicitly Demon only? As it mentions in the text in that section that it would never occur to an Angel to &quot;overload&quot; its powers like that to produce an effect (indeed doing so may cause an Angel to fall). It mentions that they can achieve similar effects (read = blatantly supernatural) with Numina. Certain Exploits do have Numina equivalents. Incendiary and Blast or Raise Dead and Resurrection for example. Hence why I believe more Angel specific Numina will be published in further Demon books to continue this trend. <br /> <br /> Also I understand that its possible to re-skin Exploits and Numina, but I would like Angels to have a distinct set of abilities from Demons. Mainly because I think it reflects the idea that Demons are &quot;running on patrol instead of nuclear&quot; that the switch from running of Essence to Aether represents. Likewise, having Angels have their own unique set of abilities in manifestations, influences and numina keeps them as more of an &quot;unknown&quot; for Demons. Who theoretically know what other Demons can do but only &quot;kinda sorta&quot; remember what they could do as Angels. <br /> <br /> Re-reading Embeds it says that Angels don't consciously use them so I guess I got the impression that for Angel's such powers were represented as Influences and Manifestations. Interesting point that they do in-fact have Embeds just use them instinctively rather then at will. Adding Embeds to Angels does make them more versatile and sets them apart from Ghosts and Spirits nicely. I may incorporate that, since I seem to have missed it completely on both my read-through's of the Core. <br /> <br /> I believe the argument as it was put to me was that Angels were first introduced in the God-Machine Chronicle to be major antagonists to Humans. Given the massive difference in powers between the base Mortal template and the Demon template (particularly with XP added) Angels were not such an issue. In so far as they were not specifically designed to be Demons antagonists by dint of predating them in concept and implementation within the game line. I believe the argument involved an idea that something like Abyssal entities from Mage were designed with Mages in mind, as a sort of &quot;counter&quot; in a way. Angels were not designed in such a way for Demons. <br /> <br /> Its not an argument I really bought into and I'm glad to re-examine it here. <br /> <br /> \u200bOne thing I do ponder is Demonic Form Abilities. If we say that Angels have Embeds and that their Influence, Numina and Manifestations roughly correspond to Exploits it appears they have no equivalent to Demon Form Abilities. As I mentioned above (if I am correct) their ephemeral nature makes them innately tougher and arguably more dynamic in their physical form but they do not have the more unique elements Demons do. Interesting, perhaps the Storytellers guide will add the option for them? Alternatively, as I mentioned previously it's easy to use the Demon system for stating Angels in the same way as Demons and just replacing Exploits with Numina and adding the different ephemeral template bits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T10:09:32-07:00","id":108301,"title":"","content":"I think you're right: Angels can (and instinctively do) use embeds, but exploits are the realm of the demon. It'll be interesting to see if they add in some numina powered abilities or examples of how to build them in the future. My opinion though is that these kind of abilities are basically GM fiat at this point - if it's interesting for the Angel to have the ability to part the red sea, they'll have a numina ability to do it. If I want to do something similiar to an exploit because it's important to the story, I'll do it. The difference between this method and a Demon exploit is that demons are supercharging an embed, while angels are just using a small matrix that may or may not be nearby, specifically built to give it this ability. When building an angel, you don't have to satisfy any prerequisites. Again, this is only my opinion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/107830-the-usage-of-high-rank-angels?p=108248#post108248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bOne thing I do ponder is Demonic Form Abilities. If we say that Angels have Embeds and that their Influence, Numina and Manifestations roughly correspond to Exploits it appears they have no equivalent to Demon Form Abilities. As I mentioned above (if I am correct) their ephemeral nature makes them innately tougher and arguably more dynamic in their physical form but they do not have the more unique elements Demons do. Interesting, perhaps the Storytellers guide will add the option for them? Alternatively, as I mentioned previously it's easy to use the Demon system for stating Angels in the same way as Demons and just replacing Exploits with Numina and adding the different ephemeral template bits.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it was very much implied that you can in fact use them to build angels, and they can manifest their angelic form if they wish. Otherwise what threat could an angel pose to a demon in one on one combat?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T10:21:16-07:00","id":108309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/107830-the-usage-of-high-rank-angels?p=108248#post108248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry, I may not have been clear enough in my post. The reference to 30+ dice was in regard to a Rank 4 or 5 Angel, as they usually have 10-15 in a stat. My argument was that while Angels might be less versatile then Demons (and I'll get onto that in a second) they pack more of raw punch at the high end of things.<br /> <br /> Yes the fact that they are ephemeral is very , very good. Please correct me if I am wrong but I do believe that even when manifested ephemeral creatures like Angels only take bashing damage from everything that is not a bane, ban or supernatural attack? Also that to properly kill one you need to drain all its essence and then fill all its corpus with agg damage. Otherwise it just reforms at the Infrastructure that spawned it (in the case of Angels).<br /> <br /> I believe I have that correct right?</div> </div> </div> </div> Close - for instance, its lethal, not agg. But you're not missing anything important.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I was under the impression that Exploits were explicitly Demon only? As it mentions in the text in that section that it would never occur to an Angel to &quot;overload&quot; its powers like that to produce an effect (indeed doing so may cause an Angel to fall). It mentions that they can achieve similar effects (read = blatantly supernatural) with Numina. Certain Exploits do have Numina equivalents. Incendiary and Blast or Raise Dead and Resurrection for example. Hence why I believe more Angel specific Numina will be published in further Demon books to continue this trend. </div> </div> </div> Angels aren't as capable of innovation as demons are. They wouldn't think to expand upon their powers like Demons would. But, that said, they can just download whatever powers they want/need from the God Machine. So, there is a strong cache of abilities angels can access. Transforming embeds + exploits into numina are just shorthand. Its something we know the G-M is capable of via occult physics, so its something the angels can do.<br /> <br /> I mean, there isn't a one-to-one correspondence. There is a thematic difference between the two, and that limits some of the less thematic options like powers that deal with Cover; that said, there's a large number of ones that are thematic for both. A fiery angel using Combustion or Incinerate isn't too unusual. Or the one ability to create Stigmatic cultists. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also I understand that its possible to re-skin Exploits and Numina, but I would like Angels to have a distinct set of abilities from Demons. Mainly because I think it reflects the idea that Demons are &quot;running on patrol instead of nuclear&quot; that the switch from running of Essence to Aether represents. Likewise, having Angels have their own unique set of abilities in manifestations, influences and numina keeps them as more of an &quot;unknown&quot; for Demons. Who theoretically know what other Demons can do but only &quot;kinda sorta&quot; remember what they could do as Angels. </div> </div> </div> That's your decision, but it doesn't impact that angels and demons do have similiar powers: they both run on occult physics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I believe the argument as it was put to me was that Angels were first introduced in the God-Machine Chronicle to be major antagonists to Humans. Given the massive difference in powers between the base Mortal template and the Demon template (particularly with XP added) Angels were not such an issue. In so far as they were not specifically designed to be Demons antagonists by dint of predating them in concept and implementation within the game line. I believe the argument involved an idea that something like Abyssal entities from Mage were designed with Mages in mind, as a sort of &quot;counter&quot; in a way. Angels were not designed in such a way for Demons. </div> </div> </div> The God Machine Chronicle book is more like Book of Spirits, or Inferno. Its a guide book for how to deal with the God Machine from a general WoD perspective. That said, Angels are as much of a Demon thing as infernals are heavily tied into Hunter, and spirits into Werewolf, and Keroberos into Geist.<br /> <br /> So, while anyone can deal with them, they're primarily tied into the themes of Demon. Just like anyone can deal with the Underworld.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bOne thing I do ponder is Demonic Form Abilities. If we say that Angels have Embeds and that their Influence, Numina and Manifestations roughly correspond to Exploits it appears they have no equivalent to Demon Form Abilities. As I mentioned above (if I am correct) their ephemeral nature makes them innately tougher and arguably more dynamic in their physical form but they do not have the more unique elements Demons do. Interesting, perhaps the Storytellers guide will add the option for them? Alternatively, as I mentioned previously it's easy to use the Demon system for stating Angels in the same way as Demons and just replacing Exploits with Numina and adding the different ephemeral template bits. </div> </div> </div> There's no equivalent for angels... because there's no reason for angels to ever be OUT of their &quot;angel form.&quot; They don't need Cover to survive. <br /> <br /> And, no, demon form abilities can be transformed into Numina or Influences as well, and used by angels. Ephemeral beings run on different principles than material beings, so those abilities manifest in different stats, Influences, and Numina, but they're still there. <br /> <br /> Most notably, I'm looking at the mind reading form power. That's something I imagine angels having.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T10:23:16-07:00","id":108313,"title":"","content":"This is literally how to run an encounter with a Rank 5 angel: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1b-bijO3uEw\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1b-bijO3uEw</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T11:16:02-07:00","id":108368,"title":"","content":"I'd just like to be clear that I think the system for making Angels is fine for allowing ST's to make Angels which are challenging and threatening to PC Demons. I'm a fan of the system. <br /> <br /> I think between the innate ephemeral traits, the inclusion of Embeds (as influences or numina) and some creative Numina (either brand new or based of other powers) Angels are plenty dangerous enough as it is. <br /> <br /> My personal preference for High Rank Angels (4 or 5) is to give them a lot of Numina that have the same effect as other powers (Exploits/Demonic Form abilities) but achieve them in slightly different ways. To go back the comparison between Incendiary (Exploit) and Blast (Numina) both end up with something getting blown to bits/set on fire (if that's blasts trapping). They have slightly different systems to get them to that effect, and I like that because it makes them feel different. I acknowledge this as a purely personal preference on my part.<br /> <br /> I think having that sort of wallup with the sheer number of dice they can roll for basic attacks and their innate ephemeral toughness is enough to compensate for say powerful Demonic Form abilities.<br /> <br /> I'm kinda focused on this issue a bit because Angels are so important for a Demon game I feel. They need to be a real danger/threat without appearing to just be ST fiat (another form of &quot;rocks fall everyone dies&quot;). The moment the players get the impression that they can &quot;take&quot; Angels on a regular basis I think Demon looses the majority of its thematic point. <br /> <br /> Interlinked to this actually is an thought I had about Bans and Banes for Angels. Considering the God-Machine rejigs its Angels between missions, do you think it would be fair to have a recurring Angel antagonist have his bane and ban altered between confrontations (if the PC's used those things to defeat him previously)? As the God-Machine &quot;adapts&quot; its servant to negate the tools of its enemy. The Angel must always have a ban and bane (due to occult physics) but the God-Machine might play around with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T11:20:07-07:00","id":108372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/107830-the-usage-of-high-rank-angels?p=108368#post108368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interlinked to this actually is an thought I had about Bans and Banes for Angels. Considering the God-Machine rejigs its Angels between missions, do you think it would be fair to have a recurring Angel antagonist have his bane and ban altered between confrontations (if the PC's used those things to defeat him previously)? As the God-Machine &quot;adapts&quot; its servant to negate the tools of its enemy. The Angel must always have a ban and bane (due to occult physics) but the God-Machine might play around with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that we have multiple examples of angels whose bans amount to &quot;cannot leave their worksite&quot; and Falling removes both ban and bane alongside the transition from ephemera to flesh, yeah, probably.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T12:11:51-07:00","id":108414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/107830-the-usage-of-high-rank-angels?p=108368#post108368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interlinked to this actually is an thought I had about Bans and Banes for Angels. Considering the God-Machine rejigs its Angels between missions, do you think it would be fair to have a recurring Angel antagonist have his bane and ban altered between confrontations (if the PC's used those things to defeat him previously)? As the God-Machine &quot;adapts&quot; its servant to negate the tools of its enemy. The Angel must always have a ban and bane (due to occult physics) but the God-Machine might play around with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to be contrary and disagree here - I would not allow it. Why? Changing a spirits ban and bane is essentially changing its fundamental nature, and it implies that the angel is adapting at an extreme level - which thematically isn't supposed to be something an angel can do without falling. When the machine creates an Angel, it creates it with a purpose in mind - the ban and bane should represent that fundamental purpose. A slight alteration might be allowed (such as saying although your ban is you can't leave your worksite - which worksite can be changed) but changing it much more than that should be tantamount to building a different angel from scratch. <br /> <br /> An angel is fundamentally a tool as far as the G-M is concerned - if it's proven ineffectual at its job, it has a choice to make: send another tool to help and change the circumstances, or get a new tool. For instance, if the hunter angels ban is discovered by the demons and they learn to exploit it to become relatively safe, the G-M might have no choice but to send in a replacement that attempts entirely new tactics. If the angel built for infrastructure construction is thwarted due to demon intervention, the G-M might decide that it's still a useful tool for what it was built for (building things) and just set it to a new project, perhaps with a guardian this time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T15:30:15-07:00","id":108659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/107830-the-usage-of-high-rank-angels?p=108309#post108309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Close - for instance, its lethal, not agg. But you're not missing anything important.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is one important thing that bears mentioning:<br /> <br /> Looking at the statblocks in GMC and Demon Core (and taking note of a specific line in the Dalga writeup), <i>virtually every sample angel in the books has Discorporate.</i> The only ones who don't are Triage (who is statless), Mister Nose, the Mirror Vulture, the Candle Maker (who, in what is probably an error, has Reaching), and the Lady in Red - all the sample angels in Demon have it.<br /> <br /> Angels are <i>really</i> hard to kill!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T15:42:38-07:00","id":108676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/107830-the-usage-of-high-rank-angels?p=108659#post108659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is one important thing that bears mentioning:<br /> <br /> Looking at the statblocks in GMC and Demon Core (and taking note of a specific line in the Dalga writeup), <i>virtually every sample angel in the books has Discorporate.</i> The only ones who don't are Triage (who is statless), Mister Nose, the Mirror Vulture, the Candle Maker (who, in what is probably an error, has Reaching), and the Lady in Red - all the sample angels in Demon have it.<br /> <br /> Angels are <i>really</i> hard to kill!</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't that effectively mean that unless you get an Angel somewhere that does not have a twlight presence (such as a Demon's bolt hole) that you basically can never permanently kill one? As the moment the fight looks lost they just Discorporate back to their Infrastructure? <br /> <br /> Though I guess the idea is to take out the Infrastructure first, thereby weakening the Angel in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T15:56:33-07:00","id":108706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oddness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/107830-the-usage-of-high-rank-angels?p=108228#post108228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This makes sense - but keep in mind that doing this changes the setting and theme of your setting. In this scenario, the god machine becomes an understandable entity rather than a malevolent, alien force. Part of the fun of making an adventure against the god machine is plotting random events that don't really make sense and never being able to get the big picture, but this changes it so that yes, one entity can and does understand what's going on.</div> </div> </div> </div> One, the angel is only a stand in; it puts a face to it, which Angels are meant to do. The God Machine is like the Internet. Its everywhere and no where. Its like... think St Michael the Archangel for the chronicle. The head of God's Army.<br /> <br /> Two, the God Machine isn't malevolent. Its a cold and uncaring machine that doesn't understand the question of morality. It can and does act to save humanity at times. Malevolent implies outright evil, of which it bluntly is not. It might not be a caring God, but its not an evil God either. <br /> <br /> Three, the random events that don't really make sense are designed to be there as part of the &quot;occult matrix&quot; (ie ritual spells), which are complex beyond normal understanding. And you don't understand it since its supposed to be the ultimate Chess Master gambit stuff. That doesn't mean you can't make allegories and metaphors to make parts of more understandable.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> None of this is changing the core setting or themes of the game. Its playing within it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T15:58:59-07:00","id":108707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/107830-the-usage-of-high-rank-angels?p=108676#post108676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Doesn't that effectively mean that unless you get an Angel somewhere that does not have a twlight presence (such as a Demon's bolt hole) that you basically can never permanently kill one? As the moment the fight looks lost they just Discorporate back to their Infrastructure?<br /> <br /> Though I guess the idea is to take out the Infrastructure first, thereby weakening the Angel in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/107830-the-usage-of-high-rank-angels?p=108676#post108676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Doesn't that effectively mean that unless you get an Angel somewhere that does not have a twlight presence (such as a Demon's bolt hole) that you basically can never permanently kill one? As the moment the fight looks lost they just Discorporate back to their Infrastructure?<br /> <br /> Though I guess the idea is to take out the Infrastructure first, thereby weakening the Angel in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div> Take out Infrastructure, use banes that destroy its essence quickly, or use the Exploit that prevents them from accessing their supernatural powers, and thereby their escape.<br /> <br /> Killing spirits of any ilk is meant to be HARD. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T19:40:26-07:00","id":108866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/107830-the-usage-of-high-rank-angels?p=108707#post108707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take out Infrastructure, use banes that destroy its essence quickly, or use the Exploit that prevents them from accessing their supernatural powers, and thereby th